          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            %em commutative diagram
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
            in which all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+morphisms"} parallel morphisms
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composition"} composing
            morphisms in the diagram agree.
          %p For example that a square diagram of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi Z
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mi g
                          %mo ′
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi f
                              %mo ′
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                        %mtd
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{&amp; X &amp; \overset{f}\rightarrow &amp; Z &amp; \\
                  g &amp; \downarrow &amp;&amp;\downarrow &amp; g'\\
                  \&amp;Y &amp; \underset{f'}\rightarrow&amp; W &amp; \\
                  }
          %p
            commutes is to say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi g
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g' \circ f = f' \circ g
            (see also at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+square"} commuting square
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#slick_definition Slick definition
          %p
            For our purposes, a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+diagram"} free diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+category"} free category
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi J
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(J) \overset{D}\to C
          %p
            Then this diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %strong commutes
            if this functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            factors (up to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≅
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext a poset
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(J) \to P \to C \;\cong\; F(J) \to C ,\; P\;\text{a poset} ;
          %p
            or equivalently (treating
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+category"} strict category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equality"} equality
            through a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi Q
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≅
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi J
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Q
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext a preorder
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J \to Q \to C \;\cong\; J \to C ,\; Q\;\text{a preorder} .
          %p
            In the above, we are identifying
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/posets"} posets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preorder"} preorder
            with certain categories in the usual ways.
          %h3#elementary_definition Elementary definition
          %p
            Recall that a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph"} graph
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %em vertices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %em edges
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t\colon E \to V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %strong free diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            of shape
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            in a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            comprises a map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and a map from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(s(e)) = s(D(e))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(t(e)) = t(D(e))
            for each edge
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ,
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s,t
            also denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/source"} source
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target"} target
            maps in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            Recall that a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path"} path
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            comprises a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/list"} list
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_0,v_1,\ldots,v_n)
            of vertices and a list
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (e_1,\ldots,e_n)
            of edges such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(e_i) = v_{i-1}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t(e_i) = v_{i}
            for each
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            is any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            (possibly zero). We say that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_0
            is the
            %strong source
            of the path and that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_n
            is its
            = succeed "." do
              %strong target
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and a diagram
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %strong composite
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/composite"} composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ;
                  %mi …
                  %mo ;
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi e
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(e_1);\ldots;D(e_n)\colon D(v_0) \to D(v_n)
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} id
                      %mrow
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \id_{D(v_0)}\colon D(v_0) \to D(v_0)
          %p
            A diagram
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %strong commutes
            if, given any two vertices
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            and any two paths
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mi p
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p,p'
            with source
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and target
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p'
            under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            are equal in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#edges_cases Edges cases
          %h3#cycles_and_loops Cycles and loops
          %p
            Cycles (including loops) are generally avoided in commutative diagrams in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            texts. However, they make sense under the definition above. For instance, commutativity of the following diagram implies that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
