            However, note that for this diagram to commute, we require the stronger condition that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = h
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mi f
                    %mo =
                    %mi h
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g f = h f
          %p
            If this is undesirable, a weaker notion of commutativity may be asked for, in which we only ask for commutativity of parallel paths where the source is a
            %strong source
            in the sense that it only has outgoing edges, and the target is a
            %strong sink
            in that it only has incoming edges. This convention may sometimes be implicitly encountered in category theory texts.
